      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The author examined the subendocardial blood flow in 79 patients with diabetes mellitus (II, II-III degree of decompensation) before and after traditional treatment. The diastolic, terminal-diastolic and average-diastolic pressures were reduced, the diastole ejection period of the left ventricle and vitality index of the myocardium were increased and were more pronounced in patients under 40 years of age after treatment indicating absence of IHD and marked atherosclerosis of the coronary arteries."},
